<h2>1. Purpose of this policy</h2>
<p>GFI-CO SARL attaches particular importance to the confidentiality and protection of the personal data of persons who visit its website or contact the company. This policy explains how personal data may be collected, used, stored and protected in connection with the use of the website <a href="https://www.gfi-co.net/">www.gfi-co.net</a>. It falls within the framework of the legislation applicable in the Republic of Côte d'Ivoire, in particular Law No. 2013-450 of 19 June 2013 on the protection of personal data.</p>

<h2>2. Data controller</h2>
<p>The controller of the personal data collected in connection with the website is:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Company name: GFI-CO SARL</li>
  {# <li>Address: [full official address to be confirmed]</li> #}
  <li>Contact e-mail: <a href="mailto:contact@gfi-co.net">contact@gfi-co.net</a></li>
  <li>Telephone: (+225) 01 43 100 250 / (+225) 07 58 835 008</li>
  {# <li>Data protection officer or contact, if applicable: [name and contact details, if applicable]</li> #}
</ul>
<p>The controller determines the purposes and means of the personal data processing carried out for the website.</p>

<h2>3. Personal data likely to be collected</h2>
<p>The data collected depends on the features used by the visitor.</p>

<h3>3.1. Contact forms and information requests</h3>
<p>When a user fills in a form, the following data may be requested, depending on the fields actually present on the website: first and last name, e-mail address, telephone number, subject of the request, content of the message, and information relating to the real estate project concerned by the request. Users are invited to provide only the information necessary to process their request. The fields actually present on the website determine the data collected.</p>

<h3>3.2. Technical browsing data</h3>
<p>When browsing the website, certain technical information may be recorded by the server or the components used, depending on their configuration: IP address, date and time of connection, pages viewed, browser type and operating system, and technical information required for the operation and security of the website. Such data must only be collected to the extent necessary for the purposes pursued and in accordance with applicable rules.</p>

<h3>3.3. WhatsApp communications</h3>
<p>The website provides a link allowing the user to open a conversation with GFI-CO SARL on WhatsApp. Simply clicking on this link redirects the user to an external service. Data subsequently transmitted or processed in connection with the conversation is subject to WhatsApp's terms and privacy policy. If GFI-CO SARL receives and retains information from such exchanges, it may also be processed to respond to the request, ensure commercial follow-up or comply with legal obligations, depending on the context.</p>

<h3>3.4. Mapping data</h3>
<p>The website may include a map using OpenStreetMap. Depending on the integration method used, viewing the map may result in the transmission of technical data, such as the IP address and information required to load mapping resources, to the servers concerned. The exact operation depends on the technical configuration of the map and any intermediary providers used.</p>

<h2>4. Purposes of processing</h2>
<p>Personal data may be processed for the following purposes:</p>
<ul>
  <li>responding to information and contact requests;</li>
  <li>reviewing quote requests or real estate projects submitted by users;</li>
  <li>ensuring follow-up of exchanges with prospects and clients;</li>
  <li>providing the information requested about GFI-CO SARL's activities and services;</li>
  <li>ensuring the operation, maintenance and security of the website;</li>
  <li>preventing fraudulent or abusive use;</li>
  <li>complying with applicable legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>Data must not be used for purposes incompatible with those brought to the attention of the data subjects. GFI-CO SARL does not currently offer a newsletter on the website. Data collected through forms must therefore not be used for automatic newsletter subscription. Any subsequent use for commercial prospecting must comply with applicable rules and, where necessary, be subject to appropriate information and consent.</p>

<h2>5. Legal basis for processing</h2>
<p>Processing is carried out on the legal basis appropriate to each situation, in accordance with applicable Ivorian legislation. Depending on the processing concerned, this basis may in particular be: the consent of the data subject, where required; pre-contractual steps requested by the data subject, in particular for reviewing a quote request or a project; compliance with a legal obligation applicable to GFI-CO SARL; or another legally applicable basis justified by the purpose pursued. Sending an information request does not automatically authorise all subsequent uses of personal data.</p>

<h2>6. Mandatory or optional nature of the data</h2>
<p>The information requested in a form must be limited to what is necessary to process the request. Mandatory fields are indicated as such on the relevant form. Failure to provide a mandatory field may prevent GFI-CO SARL from processing or properly responding to the request. Optional fields may be left blank without preventing submission of the request, where the form allows.</p>

<h2>7. Recipients of the data</h2>
<p>Personal data may be accessed, within the limits of their duties and on a need-to-know basis, by:</p>
<ul>
  <li>authorised GFI-CO SARL staff responsible for processing requests;</li>
  <li>persons responsible for commercial management or follow-up of the projects concerned;</li>
  <li>technical service providers involved in hosting, maintenance or security of the website, where necessary;</li>
  <li>competent authorities, where communication is required or permitted by law.</li>
</ul>
<p>Service providers acting on behalf of GFI-CO SARL must be bound by appropriate confidentiality and data protection obligations. Data is not intended to be sold to third parties. Any other communication must be based on a legitimate purpose and an appropriate legal basis. <strong>To be verified before publication:</strong> the recipients and service providers actually used, in particular the request transmission channel and technical providers.</p>

<h2>8. Third-party services: OpenStreetMap and WhatsApp</h2>
<h3>8.1. OpenStreetMap</h3>
<p>The website uses OpenStreetMap to display a map or facilitate the location of certain places. Depending on the integration method, requests may be sent to external servers to load mapping data or map images. These requests may transmit technical information, including the IP address, to the provider of the resources concerned. For more information, users may consult the official website <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">openstreetmap.org</a> and information from the <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/">OpenStreetMap Foundation</a>.</p>

<h3>8.2. WhatsApp</h3>
<p>The website provides a link to WhatsApp to facilitate contact with GFI-CO SARL. Users remain free to use this service or not. When they click on the link and continue the conversation, the data they transmit on WhatsApp is processed in accordance with the terms and privacy policy of that service, operated by Meta. Users may consult the official information at <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy">whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>. GFI-CO SARL does not control all processing carried out by WhatsApp. Requests addressed to GFI-CO SARL through this channel may nevertheless be processed by the company to respond to the user and ensure follow-up of the request.</p>

<h2>9. Cookies and other trackers</h2>
<p>The website may use cookies or similar technologies depending on its technical configuration. Cookies strictly necessary for the operation and security of the website may be used within the limits provided by applicable regulations. The possible use of audience measurement, personalisation or advertising cookies must be verified according to the tools actually installed on the website. Where consent is required, the trackers concerned must only be activated after valid consent has been obtained. Users must also have clear information on their purpose and on the means to withdraw consent. <strong>To be verified before publication:</strong> the presence of cookies, any analytics tools, the OpenStreetMap configuration and the existence of a preference management mechanism.</p>

<h2>10. Data retention period</h2>
<p>Personal data is retained for a period proportionate to its purpose and in accordance with applicable legal obligations. The precise periods must be determined by GFI-CO SARL according to its actual practices.</p>
{# <p><strong>To be completed before publication:</strong></p>
