<p>At the end of the relevant period, data must be deleted or anonymised, unless retention remains necessary or legally required.</p>

<h2>11. Data security</h2>
<p>GFI-CO SARL implements proportionate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against loss, destruction, alteration, disclosure or unauthorised access. These measures may include: restricting access to authorised persons; protecting systems and administrative access; updating technical components; backing up data where necessary; and managing security incidents. As no electronic transmission or storage can be guaranteed to be absolutely secure, the company strives to reduce risks according to the data processed and the resources available.</p>

<h2>12. Rights of data subjects</h2>
<p>In accordance with applicable legislation, data subjects may have rights over their personal data, including:</p>
<ul>
  <li>the right to be informed about the processing carried out;</li>
  <li>the right to access data concerning them;</li>
  <li>the right to request rectification of inaccurate or incomplete data;</li>
  <li>the right to request deletion of data under the conditions provided by law;</li>
  <li>the right to object to certain processing under applicable legal conditions;</li>
  <li>other rights recognised by applicable regulations, depending on the nature of the processing.</li>
</ul>
<p>The exercise of these rights may be subject to conditions and exceptions provided by law. Certain data may in particular have to be retained to comply with a legal obligation or to enable the exercise or defence of legal rights.</p>

<h2>13. How to exercise your rights</h2>
<p>To exercise your rights or ask a question about the processing of your personal data, data subjects may contact GFI-CO SARL:</p>
<ul>
  <li>E-mail: <a href="mailto:contact@gfi-co.net">contact@gfi-co.net</a></li>
  {# <li>Postal address: [full official address to be completed]</li> #}
  <li>Recommended subject: "Personal data request"</li>
</ul>
<p>The request must enable GFI-CO SARL to identify the processing concerned and understand the right exercised. Additional information to verify the identity of the requester may be requested where necessary and proportionate. You may also consult the <a href="https://www.autoritedeprotection.ci/">competent Ivorian data protection authority</a>.</p>

<h2>14. Data transfers</h2>
<p>The location of the hosting, the service providers and any transfers of data outside Côte d'Ivoire must be verified. Any transfer must be identified and governed in accordance with applicable rules.</p>

<h2>15. Minors</h2>
<p>The website is not specifically intended for minors. If processing concerns minors' data, GFI-CO SARL applies the protections and safeguards required by applicable legislation.</p>

<h2>16. Changes</h2>
<p>This policy may be updated to reflect changes in the website, processing practices or applicable rules. The update date is shown at the top of the page. In the event of a substantial change, data subjects are informed where required.</p>

<h2>17. Contact</h2>
<p>For any question relating to this policy or the processing of your data, please contact GFI-CO SARL at <a href="mailto:contact@gfi-co.net">contact@gfi-co.net</a>, on (+225) 07 58 835 008 or at contact@gfi-co.net.</p>
